        {
            "heading": "Choose starting era window",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "table",
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "",
                            "As of patch 2.5 , starting eras no longer require interface modding to be changed, see bookmark modding ."
                        ]
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The first two starting eras are DLC-locked, so best thing to do is to hide them by overriding interface/frontend.gui in the mod and by replacing position for picture / dlc_requirement / load_progress / label / year boxes dark_ages_window and viking_era_window windows, with:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In bookmarks.txt, give the hardcoded name from vanilla to the 3 bookmarks you want to see on the era screen:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "3rd era: name = \"BM_FATE_OF_ENGLAND\"",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "4th era: name = \"BM_THE_MONGOLS\"",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "5th era: name = \"BM_100_YEARS_WAR\"",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "You can, if needed move these around and center them, with some fitting positions."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Override the following hardcoded localization keys inside a .csv file in the localization folder of the mod:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "PICK_STARTING_ERA_TEXT",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "3rd era: BM_FATE_OF_ENGLAND, EARLY_MED, EARLY_MED_INFO",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "4th era: BM_THE_MONGOLS, HIGH_MED, HIGH_MED_INFO",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "5th era: BM_100_YEARS_WAR, LATE_MED, LATE_MED_INFO",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "For each bookmark, the 1st 6 characters defined in common/bookmarks.txt will appear, and will need to be described by adding localization keys:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "For instance with:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "then ERA_CHAR_INFO_140, ERA_CHAR_INFO_1316, ERA_CHAR_INFO_1128, ERA_CHAR_INFO_1128 and ERA_CHAR_INFO_74441 have to be localized."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Finally the era images can be customized, by overriding (or updating frontend.gui) with your own gfx: GFX_pick_era_image_3, GFX_pick_era_image_4, GFX_pick_era_image_5"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Papal succession",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In order to use Papal succession (succ_papal_succession) for another religion, the first step is to mod the sucession laws:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "A button to open cardinal screen should magically appear in the religion screen ! However clicking the button will cause a CTD, and a bit of interface modding is required:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Open domestic_religion.gui and copy the definition for window named domestic_religion_title_fraticelli_cardinal",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Create a file <my_religion>_domestic_religion.gui and paste the code.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Replace occurrences of title_fraticelli_cardinal by the new religious title defined inside folder common/religious_titles (ex: title_<my_religion>_cardinal)",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Adding a focus",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In focusview.gfx, the number of frames needs to be increased:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Add a 32*32 version of your icon in gfx/ambitions/, and reference it with spriteType name GFX_<focus_name>, <focus_name> being the new focus defined in common/ambitions/00_focuses.txt"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "In focusview.gui, add an 11th focus, and adjust its position:"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Shortcuts",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "New keyboard shortcuts can be added via shortcut = \"<key>\" . [1]"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "If using priority_shortcut flag, it will fire before any other shortcuts."
                }
            ]
        },
